Teach Howdy's recorder factory about `recording_plugin = "ir"`.

The recorder itself (recorders/ir_reader.py) is copied in verbatim by
default.nix from HritwikSinghal/svp7500-camera-fix-pack, pinned to the same
revision as ../hm1092/intel-cvs-ir. Stock Howdy 3.0.0 only ships the
opencv / ffmpeg / pyv4l2 recorders: opencv cannot read the HM1092's raw
10-bit Bayer-tagged frames, ffmpeg would debayer this physically-monochrome
sensor, and none of them drive the flood illuminator.

--- a/howdy/src/recorders/video_capture.py
+++ b/howdy/src/recorders/video_capture.py
@@ -118,6 +118,16 @@
 				self.config.get("video", "device_format", fallback="v4l2")
 			)
 
+		elif recording_plugin == "ir":
+			# Raw V4L2 reader for the HM1092 mono IR sensor on Intel IPU7.
+			# Bypasses libcamera/PipeWire, which debayer this monochrome
+			# sensor (tagged SGRBG10) and renegotiate away from 648x368.
+			# Also drives the IR flood illuminator (INT3472 owns that GPIO).
+			from recorders.ir_reader import ir_reader
+			self.internal = ir_reader(
+				self.config.get("video", "device_path")
+			)
+
 		else:
 			# Start video capture on the IR camera through OpenCV
 			self.internal = cv2.VideoCapture(
